        "Cellulitis: spreading hot tender swelling with fever through a portal (toe-web tinea, ulcer); mark the margin, elevate, flucloxacillin or IV benzylpenicillin plus flucloxacillin, treat the entry point; recurrent cellulitis in lymphoedema needs penicillin prophylaxis. Necrotising fasciitis: pain out of proportion, rapid spread, crepitus, dusky skin, toxicity — immediate surgical debridement, IV antibiotics, sepsis bundle.",
